    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for these. they're a good start but i think the score is way too low for a module this important. the script only gave me a very low coverage rating because there aren't enough individual points. \n\ncan you go much deeper? i need you to expand this significantly. break down the tests into as many granular steps and specific scenarios as possible so we don't miss anything. the more bullets you provide, the better the coverage score will be. please make it a massive list.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To achieve maximum coverage for your automated scoring, I have broken down the requirements into highly granular, exhaustive test scenarios.\n\n*   Test basic ingress/egress functionality for IPv4 packets under normal load.\n*   Test basic ingress/egress functionality for IPv6 packets under normal load.\n*   Validate successful DPI on a standard HTTP GET request (Layer 7 success).\n*   Validate successful DPI on an HTTPS handshake (Layer 7 negotiation check).\n*   Test signature detection when `malicious_signature_v4` is at the beginning of the payload.\n*   Test signature detection when `malicious_signature_v4` is in the middle of the payload.\n*   Test signature detection when `malicious_signature_v4` is at the end of the payload.\n*   Verify firewall drops traffic matching the signature across different packet sizes (small, medium, large).\n*   Test signature matching when pattern spans across sequential packets (fragment handling trigger).\n*   Verify misconfiguration handling when the signature pattern is absent but traffic is complex.\n*   Test behavior when IPv4 headers contain invalid checksums.\n*   Test behavior when IPv6 extension headers are present and valid",
      "source": "target",
